This file contains a list of potential things to do 
for future versions of TerraVision:

- Remove any dependency/reference to the $pathdotgeo
  environment variable for compiling under Windows.

- Update the Open Datasets GUI so that you can select
  an OI with a DEM (and optionally set the elevation of
  the default flat DEM that is created). Currently this
  is only possible through the command line.

- Support the same kind of request architecture used
  for http connections when doing local disk connections.
  This will have multiple request lists feeding into a
  single master request list and reader. This will get
  round the problem that under Windows you cannot open
  two copies of the same dataset because it seems that
  you cannot have different threads reading the same
  file at the same time. 

- Update the Paths/Save to Movie option with a GUI that
  lets the user specify the output image size, frame
  rate, output directory, output image format (GIF/PPM/
  JPEG), and perhaps even include the ability to 
  generate a movie film in situ.

- Look at improving the navigation interface for novice
  users, e.g. keep finger down to move instead of accel.
  Also, add a navigation mode like the VRML examine mode

- Integrate Tcl/Tk libraries into the TerraVision
  repository so that a cleaner and more robust
  connection can be made, also so that the Windows
  icon can be customized, and that those strange
  floating point Tcl error messages can be removed

- Use quaternions for all rotations - avoid that vortex
  of death behavior when navigating over the poles

- Add a feature to measure distances between points

- Add support for transaparency in terrain datasets (RGBA).
  This should largely be there already, we just need to
  do the sorting stage before rendering and then it should
  just work!!

- Update all of the stereo rendering code and make it 
  more robust and user friendly

- Support variable mesh resolutions within each DEM tile,
  perhaps doing an adaptive simplificiation scheme.

- Add support for more file format readers in tsmApi, e.g.
  add .BT support, DTED levels > 0, STDS, ArcGrid, etc.

- Support non-http proxies. Some users do not use http
  proxies to get outside their firewall, but have a direct
  socket proxy. TerraVision currently only supports http
  proxies.

- Reorganize the directory structure into something more like:
  core, ui, 3rdparty. With all directories moved under this
  hierarchy, e.g. TclTV, PluginTV, plugin, ActiveX, and XmTV
  would move under "ui".

- Solaris support. The Tcl/Tk interface has been compiled
  up and run under Solaris 2.8. There were some graphics
  artifacts which could be due to Sun's OpenGL implementation
  but that would be worth looking into. Also, the autoconf
  scripts could be a bit more Solaris aware.



